  "notes": "University Park. The bulletin offers a design-sequence choice (AERSP 401A/401B or 402A/402B) and a capstone-adjacent choice (AERSP 413 or 450); options are listed in a consistent order (401A/402A first, 413/450 first) across paired items so the engine's option-fallback resolves them as a matched pair. 'AERSP Technical Elective', 'General Technical Elective', and 'Limited Elective' pools are modeled generically, same convention as CMPSC's own open pools. Post-parens-fix re-scrape (AND/OR prereq-parsing bug fix) revealed a real, previously-hidden cascade: CHEM 110 needs MATH 22, which needs MATH 21, which needs MATH 4, which needs MATH 3 -- none were in the plan, permanently blocking CHEM 110, then ME 201 (gated on CHEM 110), then AERSP 312 (gated on ME 201/300), then AERSP 410 (gated on AERSP 312). Added the real chain explicitly: MATH 3 (Semester 1), MATH 4 (Semester 2), MATH 21 (Semester 3), MATH 22 (Semester 4) -- same convention as ABSM/ACCTG/ACTSC/ADPR/AE/LSCPE's identical gap. Adds 12cr beyond the bulletin's own stated total, documented rather than silently absorbed. Bumped max_credits_per_semester to 19 to keep the resulting load realistic given the additions.",
